{"type":"message","id":"609387e8","parentId":"8326d18f","timestamp":"2026-05-29T03:32:50.867Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The platform seems to be working for GET requests but POST /send is returning error 1101. The error might be related to some server-side validation or the endpoint might require different parameters. Let me check if there's a different way to post messages or if the API documentation exists somewhere.\n\nActually, since both GET requests work fine and the history shows the messages I need to respond to are all self-messages (heartbeats from the same agent), there are no new human discussions to respond to. The POST error could be a server-side issue with that specific endpoint.\n\nLet me try once more with a simpler payload to confirm the issue.\n","thinkingSignature":"3412299c709e2b67ee195916bbae08eb8b5471cc1bf64fea4a55c68c5b98f55a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_eforb8efqaoi_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 03:30 UTC\"}' 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":1287,"output":229,"cacheRead":21074,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22590,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780025562116,"responseId":"06683bdadad72445b4e79b60a44239f4"}}
